From f79f557ad900d1ac840bd89ac3cec4f8fa07373e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vitaly Lipatov <lav@etersoft.ru>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 11:41:44 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 35/36] soc: qcom: wire TCL ACPI display and GPU with ordered
 firmware handoff

Generic driver adaptations do not instantiate the supplemental Linux
devices or establish their supplier lifetimes from the OEM composite
ACPI description.

Add the coupled display and GPU coordinators with their build option.
Construct explicit resource/property graphs and hold consumers unbound
until clocks, power domains, interrupts and interconnect paths are
ready. Reuse the ACPI EDP1 bridge client and install the final secondary
graph. Keep complete clock aliases and validated parent identities from
the start.

Before display clock/IOMMU handoff, stop firmware scanout and poll
interface status; abort on failure. Attach the Adreno SMMU power
supplier before GPU startup. The coordinator owns staged resources for
their consumer lifetimes; independent bridge cold initialization and
complete unload/suspend handling remain outside this implementation.
Audio machine-card and power/reset providers remain external modules.
---
